ed in the centre of the town of Haugesund. It is the church for the Vår Frelser parish which is part of the Haugaland prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Vår Frelsers Church (Rogaland)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Church_of_Our_Savior%2C_spring_2019.jpg/960px-Church_of_Our_Savior%2C_spring_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Risøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.41021,"lo":5.26405,"d":382,"ds":"Risøya (or Risøy) is an island in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. The 0.23-square-kilometre (57-acre) island lies in the Karmsundet strait immediately south of the island of Hasseløya and southeast of the island of Vibrandsøya. Risøya is part of the town of Haugesund.","wpu":"Risøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Ris%C3%B8y_through_the_Ris%C3%B8ybru.jpg/960px-Ris%C3%B8y_through_the_Ris%C3%B8ybru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Skåre Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.419496,"lo":5.263322,"d":769,"ds":"Skåre Church (Norwegian: Skåre kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. It is located in the town of Haugesund. It is one of the two churches for the Skåre parish which is part of the Haugaland prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Skåre Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sk%C3%A5re_kirke_1858_Church_Haugesund_Norway_2020-06-06_DSC09436.jpg/960px-Sk%C3%A5re_kirke_1858_Church_Haugesund_Norway_2020-06-06_DSC09436.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hasseløya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.41686,"lo":5.25344,"d":928,"ds":"Hasseløya (or Hasseløy) is an island in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. The 0.3-square-kilometre (74-acre) island lies north of the island Risøya, south of the Killingøy peninsula, and between the island of Vibrandsøya to the west and the mainland to the east. Hasseløya is part of the town of Haugesund, connected to the city centre by a bridge.","wpu":"Hasseløya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Hassel%C3%B8y_bru.jpg/960px-Hassel%C3%B8y_bru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vibrandsøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.41613,"lo":5.24327,"d":1441,"ds":"Vibrandsøya or Vibrandsøy is an island in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. The island lies west of the densely built-up island of Hasseløya and northwest of the island of Risøya in the town of Haugesund. The island is now used as a recreational area.","wpu":"Vibrandsøya","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Sj%C3%B8buer_Vibrands%C3%B8y.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Karmøy (island)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.39385,"lo":5.25323,"d":2287,"ds":"Karmøy is an island in Karmøy Municipality in the northwestern part of Rogaland county, Norway. The island covers an area of 176.8 square kilometres (68.3 sq mi) and measures approximately 30 kilometres (19 mi) long, and up to 9 kilometres (5.6 mi) wide. Karmøy is the largest island in Rogaland county, the most populous island in South Norway, and the second most populous island in Norway.","wpu":"Karmøy (island)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%C3%85krasanden_05.2010_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/960px-%C3%85krasanden_05.2010_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Rossabø Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.393745,"lo":5.288459,"d":2434,"ds":"Rossabø Church (Norwegian: Rossabø kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. It is located in the southern part of the town of Haugesund. It is the church for the Rossabø parish which is part of the Haugaland prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Rossabø Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Rossab%C3%B8_kirke_fra_RA.jpg/960px-Rossab%C3%B8_kirke_fra_RA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Udland Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.438303,"lo":5.27016,"d":2816,"ds":"Udland Church (Norwegian: Udland kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. It is located in the town of Haugesund. It is one of the two churches for the Skåre parish which is part of the Haugaland prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Udland Church","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/Udland_kirke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Torvastad Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.380025,"lo":5.231749,"d":4201,"ds":"Torvastad Church (Norwegian: Torvastad kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Karmøy Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. It is located in the village of Torvastad on the northern part of the island of Karmøy. It is the church for the Torvastad parish which is part of the Karmøy prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Torvastad Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Torvastad_kirke%2C_Rogaland_-_Riksantikvaren-T238_01_0201.jpg/960px-Torvastad_kirke%2C_Rogaland_-_Riksantikvaren-T238_01_0201.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Norheim Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.379777,"lo":5.30874,"d":4355,"ds":"Norheim Church (Norwegian: Norheim kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Karmøy Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. It is located in the village of Norheim, just south of the town of Haugesund. It is the church for the Norheim parish which is part of the Karmøy prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Norheim Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Norheim_kirke.jpg/960px-Norheim_kirke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Førre Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.4243,"lo":5.38091,"d":6509,"ds":"Førre Church (Norwegian: Førre kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Tysvær Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. It is located in the village of Førre, which sits along the European route E134 highway. It is one of the two churches for the Førresfjorden parish, which is part of the Haugaland prosti (deanery) in the Diocese of Stavanger.","wpu":"Førre Church","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/F%C3%B8rre_kirke_fra_RA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Feøy","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.38434,"lo":5.15434,"d":7179,"ds":"Feøy or Føyno is a small island group in Karmøy Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. The 1.3-square-kilometre (0.50 sq mi) island group lies west of the town of Haugesund and the island of Karmøy, southeast of the islands of Røvær, and northeast of the island of Utsira. The island has 37 permanent residents, plus a number of seasonal residents and visitors who rent vacation homes.","wpu":"Feøy","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8b/Feoy_harbor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Aksdalsvatnet","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.40949,"lo":5.4213,"d":8683,"ds":"Aksdalsvatnet is a lake in Tysvær Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. The 3.46-square-kilometre (1.34 sq mi) lake lies southeast of the village of Førre and south of the village of Aksdal. The European route E134 highway runs along the northern shore of the lake and the European route E39 highway along the eastern shore of the lake.","wpu":"Aksdalsvatnet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Aksdalsvatnet.jpg/960px-Aksdalsvatnet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Haugesund ([ˈhæʉɡəsʉn] ) is a town in Haugesund Municipality in Rogaland county, Norway. The town is located along the Karmsundet strait on the southwest coast of Norway. The town lies about 60 kilometres (37 mi) north of the city of Stavanger and about 120 kilometres (75 mi) south of the city of Bergen.","wpu":"Haugesund","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Smedasundet_-_Haugesund%2C_Norway_2021-08-05_%2802%29.jpg/960px-Smedasundet_-_Haugesund%2C_Norway_2021-08-05_%2802%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}